title: $:/plugins/intertwingled-innovations/nhn/scope
tags: $:/tags/Global

\whitespace trim
\define nhn-archive-tag() Arkiv
\define nhn-draft-title-prefix() Draft of '
\function nhn-archived() [<nhn-archive-tag>tagging[]]
\function nhn-templates() [[mal]tagging[]]
\function nhn-drafts() [has[draft.of]] [has[draft.title]] [all[tiddlers]prefix<nhn-draft-title-prefix>] +[unique[]]
\function nhn-excluded() [function[nhn-templates]] [function[nhn-archived]] [function[nhn-drafts]] +[unique[]]
\function nhn-active-year() [[$:/config/nhn/active-year]get[text]] :else[[alle]]
\function nhn-in-year-scope() [function[nhn-active-year]match[alle]then<currentTiddler>] [<currentTiddler>function[nhn-year-raw]count[]match[0]then<currentTiddler>] [<currentTiddler>tag{$:/config/nhn/active-year}]
\function nhn-max-year() [<currentTiddler>tags[]regexp[^\d{4}$]sort[]last[]]
\function nhn-periodic() [enlist<nhn-governance-tags>tagging[]unique[]] [function[nhn-deliveries]] [function[nhn-objectives]] [function[nhn-results]] +[unique[]] -[function[nhn-excluded]] -[function[nhn-services]]
\function nhn-archivable() [function[nhn-periodic]] :filter[function[nhn-max-year]compare:number:lteq{$:/state/nhn/arkiv/year}]

Periodisation and archiving (brief §3.7). Two separate mechanisms, deliberately.

!! Archiving — a tag, and every selector honours it

`nhn-archived` is everything carrying the configurable `Arkiv` tag. Archiving is therefore reversible by untagging, destroys nothing, and needs no second wiki. The tag is applied in bulk from [[Arkiv]].

`nhn-excluded` is the one definition of "not content": archived tiddlers (`nhn-archived`), the `mal` templates (`nhn-templates`) and unfinished drafts (`nhn-drafts`). Every base selector — and both extract sets — subtracts this single function rather than carrying its own copy of the exclusion, so a new exclusion is one edit here, not a hunt through every filter expression.

`nhn-drafts` is a draft in TiddlyWiki's own sense: the scratch copy the editor makes while a tiddler is open. The snapshot carries 19 of them, and they are not harmless. Seven inherit the tags of what they draft, so a draft of a `Leveranse` counted as a second delivery, and a draft of a `Målsetting` as a second objective — inflating the summaries, both extracts and the OKR ToDo list against tiddlers the wiki never meant to publish. The remaining twelve lost their `draft.of` field and are recognised by title alone; they carry no tags, so they skewed nothing, but they are still listed on [[Anomalier]] so they can be deleted.

The one place archived content still counts is the ToDo lists: they answer "was the work done", and archiving a year must not turn its history into "Mangler" or blind the copy detection across the archive boundary. So `nhn-reviews-all` / `nhn-objectives-all` keep archived content, and the ToDo pages read those, while everything user-facing reads the archived-subtracting base selectors. They still subtract the templates //and the drafts//: an archived objective is work that happened, but a draft is work that was never filed, and counting one would report an objective as written when only its unsaved copy exists.

Only the **period-bearing kinds** can be archived — `nhn-periodic`: everything carrying a governance tag, plus deliveries, objectives and results. Services, divisions and templates are structural: they belong to no single year and hiding them would break the governance tree rather than tidy it.

`nhn-periodic` is deliberately wider than `nhn-reviews`, which requires a month tag. A governance-tagged tiddler with no month is still periodic content — it appears in Extract 1 — and one that could be exported but never archived would be a hole in the mechanism.

`nhn-archivable` selects everything whose //latest// year tag is at or before the chosen year, so "archive up to and including 2025" leaves alone an objective that is also tagged 2026. That is the difference between tidying and losing things.

!! Period scope — a view filter, applied only where it helps

`nhn-in-year-scope` is true when the active year is `alle`, when the tiddler carries that year, **or when the tiddler has no year tag at all**. That last clause matters: 25 deliveries, 15 objectives and 57 results are undated, and a scope that hid them would make them unreachable through navigation with no hint they existed.

The scope applies to the navigation trees only. The extracts, the ToDo lists and the summaries all carry their own period controls, and a hidden second filter silently narrowing an export would be a trap rather than a convenience.
